flowchart TB
  accTitle: The layers of the package
  accDescr: The package issue_assistant from the command line at the top to the ground: the command line in cli.py imports what runs the engine, evaluates and sets up a repository; those import the events, commands and sweeps; those the context, the comments, the application of an answer and the digest; those what reads an issue and an answer; those the settings, the languages, the engines and the client of GitHub; and those the ground of paths, constants, patterns, values and errors. A module imports only from below, and from those before it in its own layer.
  cli(["`**cli**<br>the command line`"])
  top["`**running**, **evaluation**, **accuracy**<br>**labels**, **code_scanning**, **actionlint**<br>**setup_check**, **installation**`"]
  handling["`**commands**, **events**, **sweeps**<br>what an event or a morning starts`"]
  writing["`**context**, **comments**, **applying**<br>**learning**, **digests**<br>what the engine reads, what the assistant writes`"]
  reading["`**issues**, **cleaning**, **answer**<br>what an issue says, what an answer may say`"]
  base["`**languages**, **engines**, **settings**<br>**fixture**, **github**`"]
  ground[("`**paths**, **constants**, **patterns**<br>**values**, **errors**`")]
  cli --> top --> handling --> writing --> reading --> base --> ground
